# Build context for packages/server is the REPO ROOT (see packages/server/docker-compose.yml),
# so the ignore rules have to live here — Docker only reads .dockerignore from the
# context root, and packages/server/.dockerignore is invisible to it.
#
# EVERY nested rule needs a `**/` prefix. A bare `node_modules` matches ONLY the
# context root — Docker uses Go filepath.Match, NOT gitignore semantics, so it does
# not match at any depth. Getting this wrong is not cosmetic: without `**/`, the
# host's packages/server/node_modules was copied into the image and clobbered the
# container's own pnpm install (its symlinks pointed at C:/Users/... and resolved to
# nothing on Linux), and packages/server/.env was baked into an image layer.
# `**/` matches zero or more directories, so it covers the root case too.

**/node_modules
.git
.gitignore

# Never ship secrets into an image layer. .env.example is intentionally kept —
# it holds placeholders only and documents the required variables.
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local

# Build output and caches — the image builds its own.
**/.mastra
**/.next
**/.turbo
**/dist
**/build
**/coverage
**/*.log
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Local databases and their sidecar files.
**/*.db
**/*.db-shm
**/*.db-wal

# The web package is not part of the server image.
packages/web

# Task tracker + docs — not needed to build or run the server.
.beads
docs
scripts
SPEC
README.md

**/.DS_Store
**/.vscode
**/.idea
